c9-151c983d04a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-82179" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-{90}^{∘}\\le \\theta \\le {90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/assets/d93c490adbb5cdbc0e9a09b60eea9b82ab93be8e871e334423abc17ddd62955e.png)\n\nFrom the values on the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡({300}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nHowever, ${300}^{∘}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with ${300}^{∘}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract ${360}^{∘}.$\n\n$$\n{300}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{60}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=-{60}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-82179/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2791d4-f801-5555-a859-1d373f91a67e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82179"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90536/selection/84aaba064027e7eb0bf329f6bc084c93277c0b932bcb0178f06baf24c9b9c48a" :answer/id #uuid "3368aef2-4b23-595d-8b16-5494e6310577" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90536/selection/a3f72a33bd97dbcb26e67e320a072cf6fd98f5dc94f2de44db2fa04c176254bd" :answer/id #uuid "eac8d1d3-4681-5070-ac67-8bcc76358108" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90536/selection/1a4ee89f0618612cc5673272ad35e8d4625ee9ed24d34bd6027e2e3a826aae92" :answer/id #uuid "10e2bbeb-d4ba-5a72-bd16-ab326668c099" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90536/selection/37d04d9504e3dd5572231cf73505026821eeb93b1f1f5d805ea72efcab2d0843" :answer/id #uuid "7f5001de-9a28-5808-8027-873889be49c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90536/selection/8edf36f0d0c04b8e0e3f881a66fab0f1901a06368d5ca1f6d437f77714de6bc5" :answer/id #uuid "b09a1d17-3f9e-5902-8c52-64e3ac9f8569" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90536/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "79c2aeb9-319e-5127-9c2b-5880ffe16005" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90536/selection/37d04d9504e3dd5572231cf73505026821eeb93b1f1f5d805ea72efcab2d0843" :answer-field/choices ["q-90536/selection/84aaba064027e7eb0bf329f6bc084c93277c0b932bcb0178f06baf24c9b9c48a" "q-90536/selection/a3f72a33bd97dbcb26e67e320a072cf6fd98f5dc94f2de44db2fa04c176254bd" "q-90536/selection/1a4ee89f0618612cc5673272ad35e8d4625ee9ed24d34bd6027e2e3a826aae92" "q-90536/selection/37d04d9504e3dd5572231cf73505026821eeb93b1f1f5d805ea72efcab2d0843" "q-90536/selection/8edf36f0d0c04b8e0e3f881a66fab0f1901a06368d5ca1f6d437f77714de6bc5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90536" :question/id #uuid "e68a9882-b279-53d3-a7c6-3e64592c9480" :question/math-academy-id "q-90536" :question/problem "$\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/assets/dbf36192ac332dc49ed75278838e989a37ac7d888311be1b8b059a7b59667aa6.png)\n\nFrom the values in the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\frac{7\\pi }{4}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with $\\frac{7\\pi }{4}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract $2\\pi .$\n\n$$\n\\frac{7\\pi }{4}-2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-90536/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2791d4-f801-5555-a859-1d373f91a67e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90536"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117412/selection/b9e37961d17591920349894dfae8783436f581130d0da0bd042142640bfd4f67" :answer/id #uuid "485d1a06-bc45-55d7-bc84-3ff478f6c358" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117412/selection/1e92e7e13074920ac5aa882943c0d0cc16dd496cdd41b0ca0e7d7d1595497ada" :answer/id #uuid "751c92b4-3b48-546b-902e-6679a757225c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117412/selection/f63f5b79eea3f55a3be4379cddb889f81f526ea8a521ee46369b3d5ee3259d2a" :answer/id #uuid "ee2cea99-320f-5686-80a6-703358b8b96f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{10\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117412/selection/f0f45940ed5df71758de7ff31ea171bc0689f380be113b3538530f3180b5105f" :answer/id #uuid "41e81461-54b6-55ff-bb29-74298379cdaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117412/selection/3e31db3dd3e4e9b155305930fd29ec8565b87fce6674c75b71caa215630efbf7" :answer/id #uuid "e80728a9-3025-5675-8bbd-4f6c11fc4c4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117412/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1375ee2f-e69d-5865-9f2a-987fca463960" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117412/selection/1e92e7e13074920ac5aa882943c0d0cc16dd496cdd41b0ca0e7d7d1595497ada" :answer-field/choices ["q-117412/selection/b9e37961d17591920349894dfae8783436f581130d0da0bd042142640bfd4f67" "q-117412/selection/1e92e7e13074920ac5aa882943c0d0cc16dd496cdd41b0ca0e7d7d1595497ada" "q-117412/selection/f63f5b79eea3f55a3be4379cddb889f81f526ea8a521ee46369b3d5ee3259d2a" "q-117412/selection/f0f45940ed5df71758de7ff31ea171bc0689f380be113b3538530f3180b5105f" "q-117412/selection/3e31db3dd3e4e9b155305930fd29ec8565b87fce6674c75b71caa215630efbf7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117412" :question/id #uuid "2dbc0e3f-52e0-5c91-bb08-00ee163a5979" :question/math-academy-id "q-117412" :question/problem "$10\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/assets/dbf36192ac332dc49ed75278838e989a37ac7d888311be1b8b059a7b59667aa6.png)\n\nFrom the values in the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=-1.\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract $2\\pi .$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1) & =10\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-5\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117412/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2791d4-f801-5555-a859-1d373f91a67e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117412"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117456/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d" :answer/id #uuid "d03ca6d6-79c7-53da-b39b-c3fccb4c8c2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117456/selection/8054304fddf4b48693ad35887faf99224ec7548e30e7afaf6bf777ee8da45450" :answer/id #uuid "e4883042-5eb1-59fb-9a98-e458ad0d7f31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117456/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" :answer/id #uuid "25249a7c-b142-5efb-be44-5364af701443" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117456/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" :answer/id #uuid "5202e221-fe75-56ae-a88a-eb7907338342" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117456/selection/1690f33e4dfc66b5d93932f8ce8df1d471d5c7db0590bc6354d143eec2af246a" :answer/id #uuid "af02623f-df1e-52b6-a8fb-09b2d97936df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117456/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "230471ac-8884-5482-99f0-e42d06daa657" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117456/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" :answer-field/choices ["q-117456/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d" "q-117456/selection/8054304fddf4b48693ad35887faf99224ec7548e30e7afaf6bf777ee8da45450" "q-117456/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" "q-117456/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" "q-117456/selection/1690f33e4dfc66b5d93932f8ce8df1d471d5c7db0590bc6354d143eec2af246a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117456" :question/id #uuid "c851664f-56c5-5c6e-824e-5a13456731a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-117456" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)=$" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-{90}^{∘}<\\theta <{90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and fourth quadrants.\n\nSince $1$ is positive, our answer is an angle that lies in the first quadrant, where the tangent is positive.\n\nFrom the special values of the trigonometric functions, we know that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡({45}^{∘})=1.\n$$\n\nSince ${45}^{∘}$ is an angle in the first quadrant that lies within the range of $arctan,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)={45}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-117456/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3878b5fa-fd5e-5984-8516-96ee17bf137b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117456"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-320730/field-1/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708" :answer/id #uuid "8fea6824-130d-568a-8b22-651d4b7f4508" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320730/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6baa3ed-3895-59e1-a671-f7ca80a57681" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320730/field-1/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708" :answer-field/choices ["q-320730/field-1/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf680708"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320730" :question/id #uuid "f53bc9c3-fd24-580b-be8a-fd85b0a8922e" :question/math-academy-id "q-320730" :question/problem "Expressed in degrees, $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=${{field-1}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-{90}^{∘}<\\theta <{90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and fourth quadrants.\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ is negative, our answer is an angle that lies in the fourth quadrant, where the tangent is negative.\n\nFrom the special values of the trigonometric functions and the oddness of the tangent function, we know that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-{30}^{∘})=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nSince $-{30}^{∘}$ is an angle in the fourth quadrant that lies within the range of $arctan,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})={-30}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-320730/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3878b5fa-fd5e-5984-8516-96ee17bf137b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320730"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
